'''''Elatine triandra''''' is a species of [[flowering plant]] belonging to the family [[Elatinaceae]].<ref name="POWO">{{cite web |title=''Elatine triandra'' Schkuhr {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:89520-2 |website=Plants of the World Online |access-date=15 February 2021 |language=en}}</ref> It is known by the common name '''longstem waterwort'''.<ref name="NatureServe" />

Its native range is [[Temperate]] and [[Subtropical]] Old World to Western [[Malesia]].<ref name="POWO" /> 

In New England, it's regarded as introduced and has been documented in both Massachusetts and Maine and it is found primarily around rivers.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Elatine triandra (Eurasian waterwort): Go Botany |url=https://gobotany.nativeplanttrust.org/species/elatine/triandra/ |access-date=2024-04-11 |website=gobotany.nativeplanttrust.org}}</ref>

